# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the React/Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v1.x)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with all required dependencies

### 2. Component Integration
**Modified:** `src/App.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Integrated the `<SpeedInsights />` component in the main App component
- Placed the component inside the ErrorBoundary wrapper for proper error handling

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was added following the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite applications. The component is placed at the root level of the application (inside the ErrorBoundary but after the main application providers) to ensure it captures performance metrics across all pages and interactions.

## Verification

✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run type-check`)
✅ Production build successful (`npm run build`)
✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing linting issues in UserContext.jsx are unrelated)
✅ All dependencies properly installed and lock file updated

## Next Steps

To enable Speed Insights in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Speed Insights section in your Vercel project dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate Speed Insights
4. Metrics will start appearing after the deployment receives traffic

## Files Changed
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependencies
- `src/App.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component import and integration
